// Admin surface.
//
// All RPCs in this file require USER_ROLE_ADMIN (or higher) on the caller's
// session. Authorization is enforced at the handler layer; per-RPC docs
// note any extra constraints.
//
// Scope:
//   * Worker registry — view registered workers, resolve provider
//     conflicts, force-deregister stuck workers.
//
//   * OIDC providers — read-only view of the OIDC providers users can log
//     in with. The list is configured entirely via CAIRN_OIDC_* env vars;
//     it cannot be mutated through the API.
//
//   * Instance settings — registration policy, default locale/units,
//     branding, email/SMTP test.
//
//   * User management — invite, create, suspend, delete, change role.
//
//   * Invites — generate single-use invite codes, optionally email-bound.
//
//   * Audit log — query the immutable per-action audit trail.
//
//   * Job queue — list jobs (in-flight, failed, dead-letter), retry, cancel.
//
//   * Health & maintenance — orphaned-source view, system health,
//     long-running maintenance operations.

